{"identifier":"ParkCons1938","title":"Park Conscious","description":"Elegy to recreation and relaxation in state and national parks.","videoUrl":"https://archive.org/download/ParkCons1938/ParkCons1938_512kb.mp4","thumbnailUrl":"https://archive.org/services/img/ParkCons1938","sourcePageUrl":"https://archive.org/details/ParkCons1938","durationMs":456001,"level":"B2","topic":"Recreation;Parks;Nature","sourceCredit":"Source: Internet Archive — Park Conscious","hasCaptions":true,"segments":[{"startMs":2000,"endMs":10001,"text":"Since federal help for the creation and further development of recreation areas became available through the Emergency Conservation Work Program begun in 1933,"},{"startMs":11001,"endMs":18000,"text":"it has become obvious that there is a very definite factor in the park and recreation movement which may be called park conscious."},{"startMs":18001,"endMs":26000,"text":"In some sections of the country, as in Minnesota, the public makes avid use of such outdoor recreational facilities as have been provided."},{"startMs":26001,"endMs":32001,"text":"And this very publicly expressed enthusiasm inevitably results in a more rapid development of park systems."},{"startMs":33001,"endMs":37000,"text":"Indeed, the development of parks may be said to be in direct ratio to their use."},{"startMs":38000,"endMs":45000,"text":"It is estimated that nearly a quarter million people visit eight of the principal Minnesota State Parks during the three months which constitute each summer season."},{"startMs":46000,"endMs":52000,"text":"Parks near the large centers of population in which winter sports are possible are active throughout the 12 months of the year."},{"startMs":56000,"endMs":117000,"text":"[...] more information visit www.fema. gov www.fema.gov The settings are those"},{"startMs":117000,"endMs":123001,"text":"which induce complete relaxation and rest, settings in which nature can work her magic of mental and physical healing."},{"startMs":171000,"endMs":175000,"text":"Parks are a call to the people to rest and play in family groups."},{"startMs":175000,"endMs":179001,"text":"A cure which has been seriously advocated for most of our social difficulties."},{"startMs":239000,"endMs":245000,"text":"Many of our emotions are instinctive. Certainly the thrill that comes from a boat ride is one of these."},{"startMs":245001,"endMs":247001,"text":"It lasts from childhood to old age."},{"startMs":295001,"endMs":304000,"text":"In state parks in all parts of the country there are simple but adequate facilities for camping available. Sometimes for small charges, sometimes"},{"startMs":304000,"endMs":305001,"text":"for no charge at all."},{"startMs":309000,"endMs":316000,"text":"I will leave the dust of the city street and the noise"},{"startMs":316000,"endMs":322000,"text":"of the busy town for the windy moor and the high hills and the peak stream flowing brown."},{"startMs":322001,"endMs":334000,"text":"I will keep my watch by the campfires where the white cliffs lean to the sea and dawn shall wake me with golden hands and the rain shall walk with me."},{"startMs":361000,"endMs":372000,"text":"Fishing and golfing are the hobbies of more Americans than are any other pastimes. To the fishermen, the nationwide conservation and recreation movement"},{"startMs":372000,"endMs":377001,"text":"means more places to go, more vacation hopes fulfilled, more happiness."},{"startMs":378001,"endMs":389000,"text":"Protection and propagation of wild life are important parts of the program. Every living thing, not just game in the popular sense, is considered and development"},{"startMs":389000,"endMs":391001,"text":"plans are drawn with this in mind."},{"startMs":392001,"endMs":402000,"text":"In the state parks alone, the Conservation Corps has built or improved more than 300 lakes or ponds. Many of these will be stocked with fish at regular intervals"},{"startMs":402000,"endMs":406000,"text":"and those parts, blessed with natural bodies of water, will be given the same attention."},{"startMs":407000,"endMs":418000,"text":"Minnesota needs few dams to form her glistening boots. Nature made them centuries ago, and today men go there from all corners of the country to rest and play in"},{"startMs":418000,"endMs":420000,"text":"this land of 10,000 lakes."},{"startMs":432001,"endMs":441001,"text":"State's laying the foundation for systems of parks will do well to exert every effort to so maintain and administer their recreation areas and so educate the"},{"startMs":441001,"endMs":449001,"text":"people in their use that to them will come also the happiness of the new leisure, which is so precious in this land of the sky-colored walk."},{"startMs":450000,"endMs":456001,"text":"Thank you."}]}